    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0640" n="628" xml:id="pg628"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 P.W./8–1045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-10T20:00:00+01:00">August 10, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 10—5:29 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3864. Following is text of communication handed to Minister Stucki<anchor n="46"
                        xml:id="d407-f1"/> 6 p.m. this afternoon by Japanese Minister.</p>
                <p>[Here follows text as quoted in note from the Swiss Chargé of August 10, printed
                        <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Jap Minister told Stucki that same was being transmitted through Swedish Govt to
                    British and Soviet Govts.</p>
                <p>Jap Minister also stated that English is sole official text.</p>
                <p>Stucki told me text already cabled Swiss Leg, Wash, for delivery at once to you.
                    He is giving text to Chinese Minister here for transmission to Chungking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d407-f1" n="46" xml:id="d407-f1-content">
                <p>Walter Stucki, Chief of the Foreign Affairs Division of the Swiss Federal
                    Political Department.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
